00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:12.940
As different as all organisms are, multicellular or single cell, they all share similar chemical molecules like DNA.

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:21.080
It is the DNA which determines how each performs a fundamental process, making and using energy.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:25.330
In other words, how they metabolize.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:59.760
organisms survive in this fickle and competitive universe well for one thing we all need food chemicals

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.320
we can break down and use as energy to build new cells.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.900
This apple works fine for me,

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:08.170
but it wouldn't satisfy a hungry carnivore.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:11.270
Different organisms, different energy needs.

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:18.410
No matter what the habitat a microorganism may call home,

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:22.510
all microbes are performing this one basic life process.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:28.780
A process we all must perform to survive and grow.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:37.410
Metabolism refers to the thousands of chemical reactions and physical workings of the cell.

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:40.670
It is the flow of matter and energy.

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:43.980
I'm Jim Leinfeld.

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:50.350
In this episode of Unseen Life on Earth, we'll explore a variety of energy-producing metabolic strategies.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:54.460
Strategies determined by the molecules shared by all organisms.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:59.970
DNA, the backbone of diversity, protein synthesis, metabolism...

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:02.020
and life itself.

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:09.880
Cells are like chemical factories.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.120
They spend a lot of their time producing

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.640
energy as ATP,

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:16.080
adenosine triphosphate,

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.880
the energy storage material of all life

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.360
on Earth. They then use that energy

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.380
to drive their chemical reactions.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.690
These chemical reactions

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:27.940
are divided into two groups,

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:29.940
catabolism and

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:38.030
anabolism. Catabolism is the process of breaking down macromolecules into their smaller component

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:44.960
parts. These components may either be further metabolized for energy or used as building

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:52.230
blocks for making new macromolecules. This process of using the energy and simple building

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:59.810
blocks to make new macromolecules for the cell is called anabolism. It is an organism

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.700
environment and the energy sources available in that environment that determine which energy

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:16.270
producing strategy is successful and therefore which organism will survive. Organisms can obtain

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:23.030
their energy in one of several ways such as photosynthesis, the conversion of light energy

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:29.970
into ATP or chemolithotropy, converting inorganic chemical energy such as

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:38.750
hydrogen gas or sulfur into ATP, or fermentation and respiration, the conversion of organic

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:46.700
chemical energy, such as organic waste or sugars, into ATP. They are different processes,

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:52.670
but all can go on in the same environment, and some even in the same organism, at different

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:59.980
times or under different circumstances. The way that life works is that primary...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:07.130
producers, such as photosynthetic and chemolithotrophic organisms, use part of the ATP they produce

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:14.500
to create carbon-rich compounds. Other organisms, consumers, break apart the bonds in these

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:20.820
carbon-rich compounds to release the energy that has been stored. Primary producers, such

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:27.420
as plants, form carbon-rich bonds, and consumers, such as animals and microorganisms, break

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:29.650
them. It is one big cycle.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:34.320
Microbes, since they have been here longer, have evolved more ways to do it.

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:40.110
In most of the world outside the laboratory,

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:45.290
ecosystems are complex mixtures of organisms with different metabolic abilities

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:50.730
that not only coexist, but function together to be more than the sum of the parts.

